1.Power supply failure — symptom:
PC does not power on, fans stay silent, no POST beep.  

2.RAM (memory) problem — symptom: 
random crashes or blue‑screen errors, continuous POST beep, system won’t boot. 

3.Hard drive/SSD failure — symptom:
clicking or grinding noises, Windows fails to load, files become inaccessible.  

4.Graphics card (GPU) issue — symptom:
no image on the monitor, visual artifacts on screen, driver crashes, POST beep may be absent.  

5.CPU overheating — symptom: 
sudden shutdowns or reboots, thermal throttling warnings, fan runs at full speed, system may freeze.
